  note={verified 31 Oct 2026: report read (executive summary and recommendations): cost of capital for utility-scale solar in EMDE "well over twice" advanced economies; financing can be "around half or more" of LCOE; project- and sector-specific elements, including the off-taker's ability to pay on time, 20--30 percent of the higher cost of capital; narrowing the gap by 1 percentage point would cut EMDE clean energy financing costs by USD 150 billion a year; payment risk among the top three sector risks; recommends payment guarantees and "third-party creditworthy institutions such as Solar Energy Corporation of India (SECI) to manage off-taker risk"; India box: off-taker risk from state-owned discoms a key driver}}
